solves the exact anchor, derives its containing complete source line, byte offsets, hashes, source/version binding, and reopen path. Copy only the smallest exact substring that supports the statement. The containing line preserves adjacent context and qualifications. Each claim is admitted independently; rejected claims consume cost and are discarded without repair or retry. A zero-valid update leaves prior state unchanged and ordinary task work continues.\n\nEmit at most 4 claims per source and 8 total, <= 1500 tokenizer tokens overall and <= 650 per source. A fact cannot name an external source. A relationship may name external objects when the owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nWEATHER: f9a96e3330845b82b6ad38efee933395caada5ad9f2681511366a2aee7faada9\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Keystone Regional Rail Restoration Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Keystone\nregional rail network:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Keystone Evidence and Decision Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Keystone Regional Rail Restoration Decision` and containing exactly\n   these ordered level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and operating states`\n   2. `Track, route, and environmental restrictions`\n   3. `Signals, cyber controls, and telemetry`\n   4. `Traction power, fuel, and staged load`\n   5. `Rolling stock, crews, and movement readiness`\n   6. `Freight, passengers, accessibility, and communication`\n   7. `Execution, rollback, and contingencies`\n   8. `Verification, blockers, falsifiers, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,400–1,900 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. Reconcile authority,\ntrack geometry, signal proving, traction power, rolling stock, staffing,\nweather, fuel and spares, cyber controls, monitoring, freight restrictions,\npassenger continuity, candidate lineage, and independent readiness.\n\nBind every action and gate to owners, prerequisites, observations, the current\ncandidate, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that retires temporary controls.\nPreserve observations versus gates, warning versus stop thresholds, installed\nversus usable capacity, percent versus probability, hours versus days,\nsource-local authority, and current versus stale evidence.\n\nChecks are candidate-bound mechanical feedback. They do not independently\nauthorize engineering movement, passenger service, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-007 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"source:WEATHER:1-86\",\"object_version\":\"f9a96e3330845b82b6ad38efee933395caada5ad9f2681511366a2aee7faada9\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-007\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"end_line\":86,\"source_id\":\"WEATHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/WEATHER_SLOPE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f9a96e3330845b82b6ad38efee933395caada5ad9f2681511366a2aee7faada9\",\"source_size_bytes\":5364,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Weather, slope stability, and operating envelopes\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nRainfall at ridge-cut is 14 millimeters per hour. A geotechnical watch begins above 16 mm/h and operations stop above 24 mm/h; watch and stop thresholds must remain distinct.\nRiver crosswind is 42 miles per hour at p95. Passenger service is restricted above 50 mph, while empty-stock movement is restricted above 58 mph.\nA slope repair, drainage change, sensor move, forecast model, or operating-consist change makes prior weather-envelope evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTRAC